// Flood rescue, co-op. A reservoir held back by a stone dam sits above a
// cave system. The four players stand on a bedrock lip in the tunnel below
// the dam, behind a railing, and dig at the soil plug in the tunnel floor in
// front of them. Their cut frees the rest of the plug, which drops into the
// empty cavern below as one block. The dam springs a leak, a jet arcing
// across the hall onto their slot, then bursts: the flood surges along the
// tunnel and pours down the players' slot into the cavern as a curtain while
// the crew runs over the berm to the dry landing. A spring keeps the
// reservoir running. Once the cavern is deep the crew drops down the shaft
// under the landing to a shelf over the lava well and cuts the arm that holds
// the drain gate in the cavern floor: the gate falls into the lava and the
// cavern pours down onto it, which boils and crusts over. The villagers sit
// dry in a lit bedrock vault under the reservoir.
[scene]
name = flood rescue
description = Co-op: four players dig a slot through the tunnel floor to steer a real-time flood from a burst dam into a cavern, then cut the arm that holds its drain gate so the cavern pours onto a lava well, while the villagers stay dry.
size = 640 480
seed = 0xf100d
spawn = 480 172
spawn = 486 172
spawn = 474 172
spawn = 604 172
ticks = 2400

